# Hypothesis / claim (before recommendations)

**Triggers.** Hypothesis · claim · because · kill condition · rival hypothesis · root cause ·
“this is the root cause” · we believe · would be wrong if.

## Gate — do not write the claim yet if…

| Still open | Do this instead |
|---|---|
| Frame / problem not chosen | Framestorm → problem statement |
| Problem statement not locked | `.cursor/rules/problem-statement.mdc` |
| Priorities / issue branches not set | MECE tree + prioritize |
| Answers not vetted to **where the problem is** | Research / falsifiers first |

**Before any recommendation**, the team must be able to say:  
**“This is the root cause of the problem.”**  
(That is a location of the constraint — still not “therefore buy SynELISA.”)

Only then write the working claim.

## Required claim shape (four parts)

1. **Claim with a because that can fail** — specific mechanism, not a slogan  
2. **Evidence that puts it first** — why this claim, not a sibling  
3. **Decision change** — what Synvitta does **differently** if this is right  
4. **Kill condition** — what observable result would prove it wrong  

### Template (use this form)

> We believe **[customer or partner type]** would **[buy / evaluate / co-develop]** within 90 days
> **because** ___.  
> Evidence that puts it first: ___.  
> If right, Synvitta does differently: ___.  
> We would be wrong if ___.

The because must be **able to fail**. If nothing could falsify it, rewrite.

## Two test horizons (both required)

| Horizon | What “testable” means | Example style (not a locked claim) |
|---|---|---|
| **Next ~4 hours** | Can be checked in the case work window (desk research / case facts) | e.g. no named U.S. buyers of comparable products; no public RUO listing; Brazil transfer fact missing |
| **90 days** | Only observable after real outreach / eval / partner motion | e.g. no eval started; no SOW; counterpart refuses under claim rules |

Every serious hypothesis needs **at least one 4-hour kill** and **at least one 90-day kill**.  
Prompt-card style: mark whether the kill is observable in three hours, in 90 days, or neither — “neither” fails.

## Rival on the same branch (strong teams)

On the **same** prioritized branch, write a **rival hypothesis** that competes on mechanism
(not a rewording). Test both. MECE: rivals are mutually exclusive explanations; do not “both win”
without splitting the branch. See `.cursor/rules/mece.mdc`.

## Hard rules

- **Before recommendations** — no “therefore the one opportunity is X” until root cause is stated and
  the claim’s because can fail.
- Do not smuggle the product pick into the because as if it were evidence.
- Align with PS goals: **90-day movability** and **value of being right**.
- Case outs still hold (no FDA filing strategy, forecast, national TAM).

Working files: `Framing/hypothesis-template.md` → `Framing/hypotheses.md` when the stage opens.

**When the team announces root cause + claim drafted:** follow `.cursor/rules/decision-routing.mdc`
— next is **analysis test** (`.cursor/rules/analysis-test.mdc`), not the recommendation. Each
hypothesis must map to issue-tree branch(es) and a work-plan row.
